### 4. JSON-LD Event Structured Data

**File:** `frontend/src/pages/EventDetailNew.jsx`

Every event detail page now includes a `schema.org/Event` block in the HTML source. This is what enables **Google Rich Results** — enhanced search listings that show date, venue, and price directly on the search results page.

**Data injected per event:**

```json
{
  "@type": "Event",
  "name": "Event Title",
  "description": "First 160 characters of event description",
  "startDate": "2026-05-20",
  "image": "https://cdn.../event-poster.jpg",
  "url": "https://www.indulgeout.com/events/event-slug",
  "location": {
    "@type": "Place",
    "name": "City Name",
    "address": { "addressLocality": "Mumbai", "addressRegion": "Maharashtra" }
  },
  "organizer": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Community/Organizer Name"
  },
  "offers": {
    "@type": "Offer",
    "price": 499,
    "priceCurrency": "INR",
    "availability": "InStock"
  }
}
```

**Why it matters:** Google can surface events directly in search under the "Events" rich result carousel — this shows the event name, date, venue, and price without the user even clicking. Significantly higher click-through rates.

